    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        67.39069366455078,
        527.4466552734375,
        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "focus of the analysis was to compare how the two tests performed in terms of predicting treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        149.60739135742188,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "failure or relapse.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        102.29462432861328,
        527.4004516601562,
        116.73762512207031
      ],
      "text": "The main findings of the analysis were that monthly culture had a higher sensitivity than monthly",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        115.49463653564453,
        527.4222412109375,
        129.93763732910156
      ],
      "text": "smear microscopy (0.93 vs 0.51) but slightly lower specificity (0.97 vs 0.99). Likewise, the sensitivity",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        128.69459533691406,
        527.4300537109375,
        143.13758850097656
      ],
      "text": "of culture done every month was much higher than once every 2 months (0.93 vs 0.73) but had a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.4365234375,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "slightly lower specificity (0.97 vs 0.98). Monthly culture increased the number of patients detected",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.423583984375,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "with a true positive bacteriological result by 13 per 1000 patients and reduced false negative results",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        168.29469299316406,
        527.3793334960938,
        182.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "by 13 per 1000 patients when compared with sputum smear microscopy alone. In contrast, monthly",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        181.4947052001953,
        527.3192749023438,
        195.9376983642578
      ],
      "text": "culture was estimated to lead to 17 per 1000 fewer true negative results and 17 per 1000 more",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.69471740722656,
        527.4135131835938,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "false positive results for treatment failure, implying that treatment may be prolonged in the case of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        207.8946075439453,
        527.44091796875,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "false positivity or missed true negativity. The added inconvenience to the patient and programme is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.09474182128906,
        527.3738403320312,
        235.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "considered relatively small, given that taking sputum and many other biological specimens is usually",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        234.29469299316406,
        527.4519653320312,
        248.73768615722656
      ],
      "text": "non-invasive and routine practice in many programmes. In a setting where testing is repeated at",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        247.4947052001953,
        527.4036254882812,
        261.9377136230469
      ],
      "text": "monthly intervals, a single false positive test result is unlikely to prove harmful to the patient because",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        260.6947021484375,
        527.4168090820312,
        275.1377258300781
      ],
      "text": "treatment decisions usually rely upon at least two consecutive positive results (to denote prolonged",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        273.89459228515625,
        527.39697265625,
        288.3376159667969
      ],
      "text": "positivity or reversion) and the effect of one spurious result would last only until the test repeated",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        287.0947265625,
        188.33731079101562,
        301.5377502441406
      ],
      "text": "1 month later is reported.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        308.798583984375,
        527.2328491210938,
        323.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "The crude odds of treatment failure increased steadily with each additional month without",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        321.99859619140625,
        527.43115234375,
        336.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "bacteriological conversion, from 3.6 at the end of the first month to 45 at the eighth month when",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        335.088623046875,
        527.388427734375,
        349.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "Table 5.1 using culture ( ). However, no discrete cut-off point (to serve as a reliable marker of a failing",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        348.39862060546875,
        527.44873046875,
        362.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "regimen) could be discerned at which the odds of failure increased sharply when monitoring with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        361.5986022949219,
        527.235595703125,
        376.0416259765625
      ],
      "text": "either sputum smear microscopy or culture. The threshold for when to change treatment thus depends",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.954907417297363,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        374.7986145019531,
        527.37060546875,
        389.24163818359375
      ],
      "text": "on the clinician’s desire to minimize the risk of failure and, in particular, to limit the risk of prolonging",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        387.99859619140625,
        149.91757202148438,
        402.4416198730469
      ],
      "text": "a failing regimen.",
